Design references: retained credit without source-license scope
---------------------------------------------------------------

Side-by-side comparison and the recorded development provenance found no
adapted source expression in these groups:

- HOL Light wf.ml and ind_types.ml: wfrec.rhm, treerep.rhm, and
  datatype_rec.rhm use distinct recursion and path-indexed-tree constructions.
- HOL4 src/bool/boolScript.sml: bool.rhm uses the same published choice of
  ETA_AX, SELECT_AX, and BOOL_CASES_AX, not HOL4 implementation expression.
- ACL2 prove.lisp, other-processes.lisp, simplify.lisp, and induct.lisp:
  waterfall.rhm, goal.rhm, simp.rhm, destruct.rhm, fertilize.rhm, general.rhm,
  irrelevance.rhm, induct.rhm, order.rhm, ruledb.rhm, plus hint handling in
  elab.rhm and driver.rhm, share architecture and terminology only.
- QuickCheck Gen.hs and Test.hs: generator/shrinker emission in
  module_block.rhm is an independent implementation.

Accordingly, those files are 0BSD. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/HOL4.txt,
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/ACL2.txt, and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/QuickCheck.txt retain the
upstream copyright notices, authorship, exact audit revisions, and terms as
provenance records; BSD-3-Clause is not asserted as a license of the package
source. Related tests and documentation are also 0BSD unless they contain
independently identified adapted expression.
